      "frases": [
        {
          "es": "Cuando Horus y Set discutían ante los dioses, un dios con cabeza de pájaro anotaba cada palabra.",
          "en": "When Horus and Set argued before the gods, a god with a bird's head wrote down every word."
        },
        {
          "es": "Era Thoth, el escriba de los dioses.",
          "en": "This was Thoth, the scribe of the gods."
        },
        {
          "es": "Los egipcios lo llamaban Djehuty y lo dibujaban con cabeza de ibis, un ave de pico largo y curvo.",
          "en": "The Egyptians called him Djehuty, and drew him with the head of an ibis, a bird with a long, curved beak."
        },
        {
          "es": "A veces era un babuino, un mono de cara larga que grita al amanecer, como saludando al sol.",
          "en": "Sometimes he was a baboon, a long-faced monkey that shouts at sunrise, as if greeting the sun."
        }
